ory holding periods, or even a "blackout window" before major announcements—we can shrink that head start even further. So I'll concede this to you: yes, it's not perfectly fair. But perfect fairness is not achievable in any market. What we can achieve is a market that is more honest, more transparent, and ultimately more efficient—and that benefits everyone, including the average person, in the long run.
